---
import { supportEmail } from "../config/contact";
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
    title="Terms of Service"
    description="The rules for creating accounts, participating in events, and using AReach’s live discovery features."
    lastUpdated="August 31, 2026"
>
    <section>
        <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
        <p>
            These Terms of Service govern your use of the AReach application,
            website, and related services. By using AReach, you agree to these
            Terms and the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not
            agree, do not use the service.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>2. Eligibility and accounts</h2>
        <p>
            AReach is intended for professional event participants and is not
            directed to children under 13. You are responsible for providing
            accurate account information, protecting your password, and all
            activity performed through your account. Do not share your password
            or authentication codes with another person.
        </p>
        <p>
            You must notify us promptly if you believe your account has been
            accessed without permission. We may suspend access when necessary
            to protect users, events, or the service.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>3. Events and user content</h2>
        <p>
            Event hosts are responsible for providing accurate event
            information and sharing invite codes only with the people they
            intend to invite. Participants are responsible for the information
            they choose to include in their profiles and events, including
            names, headlines, “Ask me about…” topics, titles, descriptions,
            venues, and schedules. Submit only content that you have the right
            to provide and that you are comfortable sharing in the relevant
            event.
        </p>
        <p>
            AReach displays eligible attendee information within the relevant
            event to support face-to-face discovery. You retain your rights in
            the content you provide, and grant AReach the limited permission
            needed to store, process, and display it to provide the event and
            attendee features you use. Do not use AReach to collect, copy, or
            distribute another participant’s information outside the event
            without their permission.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You may not use AReach to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Harass, threaten, impersonate, stalk, or discriminate against
                another person.
            </li>
            <li>Share unlawful, abusive, misleading, or infringing content.</li>
            <li>
                Attempt to access events, accounts, credentials, or data without
                authorization.
            </li>
            <li>
                Reverse engineer, disrupt, overload, or interfere with the
                service or nearby-device protocols.
            </li>
            <li>
                Use the live camera experience in a dangerous situation,
                including while driving or operating machinery.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>5. Camera and nearby features</h2>
        <p>
            The live experience depends on compatible Apple hardware, ARKit
            tracking, camera access, Bluetooth or Local Network access, Nearby
            Interaction permissions, event membership, and the availability of
            other participating devices. These features may be limited,
            interrupted, or unavailable in some environments. AReach does not
            guarantee that every attendee will be detected or that every
            overlay will appear continuously.
        </p>
        <p>
            You control whether to grant the relevant iOS permissions. The live
            camera feature processes camera frames on-device and is not a
            substitute for ordinary awareness of your surroundings.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>6. Safety tools and privacy controls</h2>
        <p>
            You can report another attendee from within a live event and choose
            a reason such as inappropriate profile content, harassment or
            abusive behavior, impersonation, spam, or other. AReach may review a
            report and may take reasonable action, including limiting,
            suspending, or terminating access when necessary to protect users or
            the service. We do not guarantee a particular response time or
            outcome.
        </p>
        <p>
            You can block an attendee and later manage your blocked users from
            the app. A block hides the two users from each other in AReach
            discovery and nearby profile presentations. You can also control
            whether your profile is visible to nearby attendees. See the{" "}
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for the details of these
            controls and the information AReach processes.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
            AReach and its software, branding, design, and service materials are
            owned by AReach or its licensors and are protected by applicable
            intellectual-property laws. These Terms give you a limited,
            non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the service for its
            intended purpose.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>8. Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
            We may change, suspend, or discontinue parts of AReach, including
            individual event or nearby-discovery features. We may update these
            Terms when the service or legal requirements change. The updated
            version will be posted on this page with a new date.
        </p>
        <p>
            AReach is provided on an “as available” basis. To the extent
            permitted by law, we do not guarantee that the service will be
            uninterrupted, error-free, or available on every device or network.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>9. Ending use and account deletion</h2>
        <p>
            You may log out or stop using AReach at any time. Logging out or
            stopping use does not by itself delete your account or stored event
            history. To permanently delete your account, use{" "}
            <strong>Profile → Account → Delete Account</strong> in the app. The
            deletion process and any study-record exception are described in
            the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            We may suspend or terminate access if you violate these Terms,
            create a security or safety risk, or if continued access is no
            longer practical. Sections that should reasonably survive
            termination, including privacy and intellectual property, will
            continue to apply.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Questions about these Terms can be sent to{" "}
            <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</LegalLayout>
